      "writtenOn": "2022-06-16T14:39:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think the implementation requires it, it just means that if you\u0027re not a multiple of your grid dimensions, then the grid cell size maps to partial pixels. That\u0027s maybe a little weird, but not problematic, and seems friendlier if someone just wants to always use a 128x128 grid for instance.\n\nIn MakeRes() I opted to round up the device bounds to be a multiple just so that the grid cell size matched what was requested, vs. shrinking slightly if it weren\u0027t a multiple.\n\nwhat do others think?",
